{"wikidata":{"entityId":"Q171529","revision":2553284075,"retrievedAt":"2026-10-15T05:06:42.591Z","labels":{"en":"canoe","tr":"Kano"},"descriptions":{"en":"light boat that is paddled"},"titles":{"enwiki":"Canoe","trwiki":"Kano"}},"encyclopedia":{"title":"Canoe","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379716433","attribution":"Wikipedia contributors, Canoe","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","termsReference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Copyrights","retrievedAt":"2026-10-15T05:08:04.810Z","extract":"A canoe is a lightweight, narrow watercraft, typically pointed at both ends and open on top, propelled by one or more seated or kneeling paddlers facing the direction of travel and using paddles.
In British English, the term canoe can also refer to a kayak, whereas canoes are then called Canadian or open canoes to distinguish them from kayaks. However, for official competition purposes, the American distinction between a kayak and a canoe is almost always adopted. At the Olympics, both conventions are used: under the umbrella terms Canoe Slalom and Canoe Sprint, there are separate events for canoes and kayaks.

"}}

{"wikidata":{"entityId":"Q228039","revision":2557038733,"retrievedAt":"2026-10-15T05:06:42.591Z","labels":{"en":"lock","tr":"kilit"},"descriptions":{"en":"mechanical or electronic fastening device","tr":"mekanik veya elektronik sabitleme cihazı"},"titles":{"enwiki":"Lock and key","trwiki":"Kilit ve anahtar"}},"encyclopedia":{"title":"Lock and key","reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?oldid=1379921063","attribution":"Wikipedia contributors, Lock and key","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0","termsReference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Copyrights","retrievedAt":"2026-10-15T05:08:08.261Z","extract":"A lock is a mechanical or electronic fastening device that is released by a physical object (such as a key, keycard, fingerprint, RFID card, security token or coin), by supplying secret information (such as a number or letter permutation or password), by a combination thereof, or it may only be able to be opened from one side, such as a door chain.
A key is a device that is used to operate a lock (to lock or unlock it). A typical key is a small piece of metal consisting of two parts: the bit or blade, which slides into the keyway of the lock and distinguishes between different keys, and the bow, which is left protruding so that torque can be applied by the user. In its simplest implementation, a key operates one lock or a set of locks that are keyed alike, a lock/key system where each similarly keyed lock requires the same, unique key.

